# L §5.12 Sides (round 12): "A key whose membership in a side is a hole (its binding's day, span or where a hole,
# §5.7) takes part with every arc of it a hole condition carrying those questions"; Holes: "A take is 0 wherever its arc
# is false, or R_s or Q_d is known to be 0, whatever the other side: on a known arc as on an arc whose condition is a
# hole. Otherwise a hole side, or a hole condition, makes the take a hole." d0 is a stated hole and ana is alive (L §5.7):
# ana's arc in f is a hole condition, its take the hole; in g the demand is known to be 0, so the take is 0.
# (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.12, writer 5's T-61.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind persons

input d0: date
input cap: money PLN
input need: money PLN
input none_needed: money PLN

fill f
  supply cap for p in persons on d0
  demand need
  arc true
  order cap

fill g
  supply cap for p in persons on d0
  demand none_needed
  arc true
  order cap

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d0 = ?"which day?"
  cap = 100.00 PLN
  need = 50.00 PLN
  none_needed = 0.00 PLN
  persons + [ana] lives 1990-01-01..

ask t1: f.taken[ana] law 2026-06-30
ask t2: g.taken[ana] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
t1: ?"which day?" (d0)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
t2: 0.00 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
